BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0 0 0 rg 246.8 518.0 Td (Stateless firewalls lack connection-tracking tables \(conntrack\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0 0 0 rg 70 505.0 Td (They evaluate every packet in isolation. When a client initiates inbound HTTP/HTTPS traffic from an) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0 0 0 rg 70 492.0 Td (ephemeral port \(1024-65535\) to port 80/443, the inbound packet is permitted. However, the return HTTP) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0 0 0 rg 70 479.0 Td (response has destination port equal to the client's ephemeral port. Without explicit outbound rules) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0 0 0 rg 70 466.0 Td (allowing TCP 1024-65535 to 0.0.0.0/0, return packets are dropped.) Tj ET
