BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0 0 0 rg 246.8 453.0 Td (NACLs evaluate rules sequentially in ascending numerical order,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0 0 0 rg 70 440.0 Td (stopping on the first match. To block the abusive block 198.51.100.0/24 on all ports \(including web) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0 0 0 rg 70 427.0 Td (ports\), the deny rule was assigned Rule 50. If placed after the allow-all web rule \(Rule 100\), malicious) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0 0 0 rg 70 414.0 Td (traffic on port 80/443 would match Rule 100 first and bypass protection.) Tj ET
